    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "is the fraction of biochar that is not present as\r\ninertinite and may degrade if exposed to ambient\r\natmospheric conditions.\r\nis the total mass of biochar mixed into the\r\nconcrete.\r\nis the total mass of the inertinite\r\nfraction of the biochar mixed into concrete.\r\nFLabile\r\nmBiochar,total\r\nmBiochar,inertinite\r\nFor biochar production, the calculation of\r\nis determined by the requirements\r\nlaid out in Section 2 of the Biomass Feedstock Accounting\r\nModule.\r\n7.2.2\r\nCalculation of CO2eCounterfactual,RP\r\nCO2eCounterfactual, RP\r\nis the total greenhouse gas emissions\r\nassociated with a given Reporting Period, RP.\r\nEquations and emissions calculation requirements for\r\nincluding emissions associated with\r\nreactor operations and reaction monitoring, are set out in\r\nthe relevant Protocol and are not included in this Module.\r\nSpecific considerations for CO stored as biochar in built\r\nmaterials are set out here.\r\nCO removals must not be double counted, regardless of the\r\nproduction of product Environmental Product Declarations.\r\nThe product must still comply with all relevant emission\r\naccounting regulations and requirements, which may mean\r\nemissions are double counted, however removals must not\r\nbe double counted. This is the most conservative approach\r\n7.2.3\r\nCalculation of CO2eEmissions,RP\r\nCO2eEmissions, RP\r\nCO2eEmissions, RP\r\n2\r\n2\r\n03/02/2026, 10:56 Biochar Storage in the Built Environment v1.0 — Isometric\r\nhttps://registry.isometric.com/module/biochar-storage-built-environment/1.0 37/70"
